{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands API support and introduces Cross Region Inferencing for OpenAI models - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has expanded its API support to include OpenAI GPT-5.6 models (Sol, Terra, and Luna) on the bedrock-runtime endpoint, with compatibility for the Responses, Converse, and Chat Completions APIs. The update introduces cross-region inference, allowing customers to access higher throughput and lower inference costs by automatically routing requests across multiple AWS Regions. Geo cross-region inference keeps data processed within a specific geography, while Global cross-region inference serves requests from any commercial AWS Region where the model is available. This launch also expands API support for OpenAI models, enabling usage of the Responses API, Chat Completions API, and Converse API on the bedrock-runtime endpoint. Cross-region inference for OpenAI models is now available in all AWS Regions where OpenAI models on Amazon Bedrock are offered. Usage is logged and can be attributed to model invocation logging, Amazon CloudWatch metrics, AWS Cost Explorer, and the AWS Cost and Usage Report. Cross-region inference for OpenAI models is available in all AWS Regions where OpenAI models on Amazon Bedrock are offered. To get started, review the model cards for GPT 5.6 (Sol, Tera, and Luna) in the Amazon Bedrock User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/amazon-bedrock-cross-region-openai-v2/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing a base model to customize or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the model catalog, checking data quality (duplicates, languages, PII), transforming or validating data (reformat, clean, filter, dedupe, split, merge, redact), generating synthetic data, labeling data with a model, human review or annotation and applying its corrections, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for SageMaker Ground Truth labeling jobs, Feature Store, or general AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"arc-region-switch","skill_description":"Answers questions about Amazon Application Recovery Controller (ARC) Region switch including architecture, plans, execution blocks, workflows, triggers, active/active vs active/passive, cross-account support, recovery time, dashboards, and customer positioning. Applicable when users ask about ARC Region switch adoption, design, or troubleshooting.\n\nServices: arc-region-switch\nTasks: learn, architect, build, debug, migrate, advise\nPersona: developer, devops, solutions-architect\nWorkload: disaster-recovery, multi-region\n*","skill_name":"arc-region-switch"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs on Bedrock cross-Region inference pricing and considerations"}
